    "created_at": "2019-08-14T12:30:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-14T14:07:11Z",
    "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-rules-for-choosing-a-browsing-context-given-a-browsing-context-name needs to be changed to always allow for creating a new browsing context as a UX decision.\r\n\r\nThe current wording isn't even adequate for cmd+click. I suspect we basically want to give maximum freedom to browsers over the chosen browsing context as the distinction between the empty string and `_self` is only meaningful here, it's not with cmd+click.\r\n\r\n(As far as I can tell #4197 did not regress this. It was broken then too.)",
